# Copy to .env. Everything here is read by docker compose — and ONLY by docker
# compose.
#
# The ramp itself has no knobs any more. MAX_RATE, RAMP_SECONDS, CONNECTIONS,
# TIMEOUT_S, REQ_PATH, PROXIES and COOLDOWN are compiled into the c1k and c10k
# profiles in bench/src/profile.zig, because the fairness contract of this
# benchmark is "never compare runs with different ramp parameters" and eleven
# environment variables with silent `catch default` fallbacks is how a real run
# executed with TIMEOUT_S=0 against a documented 1 with nothing noticing.
#
# The per-profile proxy tuning (ZOXY_CONN_SLOTS, ZOXY_UPSTREAM_SLOTS) is also in
# profile.zig and is passed to compose by `bench suite`; the entries below are
# for driving compose BY HAND.

# --- the fairness box: identical for every proxy (hard invariant) -----------
# Every proxy is hard-capped to 1 CPU (one thread/process) and pinned to core 0
# by the cloud overlay — the thread knobs are hardcoded to 1 in each proxy's
# config, so there is no PROXY_CPUS knob.
PROXY_MEM=512m
BACKEND_CPUS=4        # >=2x the proxy so the origin is never the bottleneck
BACKEND_MEM=1g

# --- filled in by bench suite; set by hand only for a manual compose run ------
#BACKEND_IP=          # zoxy does no DNS, so the origin must be an address
                      # literal — compose interpolates this into every proxy's
                      # extra_hosts and into pingora's BACKEND_ADDR

# --- zoxy build ---------------------------------------------------------------
ZOXY_REF=1735ed7a7c2ea22e8786a83ec8309cdd80760484  # pinned SHA of zoxy-io/zoxy
                      # main tip as of 2026-07-28 (one commit past 534152f).
                      # #109 adds timeouts.request_ms (config.template.json
                      # sets it to 200): a cap on one L7 exchange, from the
                      # request head being routed to the last response byte —
                      # NOT refreshed by activity like idle_ms, so it bounds a
                      # request that's merely slow, not only one that has
                      # stalled. 0 (the default) disables it. Direct fallout
                      # from our own #108 c10k run: pinning the upstream
                      # ceiling to the conn ceiling drove shedding to ~0 but
                      # left nothing bounding an overloaded exchange at all —
                      # zoxy's own before/after (22,568->0 sheds, throughput
                      # flat) showed connection churn tripling and 140,947
                      # served-but-abandoned responses (loadgen had already
                      # timed out and moved on). Expires into a 504 with no
                      # body sent, or a teardown if a response was already in
                      # flight. Smoke-tested locally (config parses, zoxy
                      # starts and serves 200s; conn-slot footprint ticked up
                      # 8B/slot for the new per-connection deadline field —
                      # 290,899->290,988 KiB at conn_slots=upstream_slots=
                      # 11464) against this repo's config.template.json/
                      # entrypoint.sh before use. #108 (prior pin) pinned the
                      # upstream-pool ceiling to the conn-slot ceiling — both
                      # now 11464 (was 12282/8192) — because an upstream is
                      # leased for a whole client exchange, not per in-flight
                      # request, so a conn_slots_max above upstream_slots_max
                      # was admission capacity that couldn't be served. Pin a
                      # SHA — the Dockerfile caches the git clone, so a branch
                      # name like "main" would silently be a stale commit.
#ZOXY_OPTIMIZE=       # zig build mode for the zoxy image (default ReleaseFast)
#ZOXY_CONN_SLOTS=     # runtime limits.conn_slots / limits.upstream_slots. The
#ZOXY_UPSTREAM_SLOTS= # profiles set these (c1k 1386/1386, c10k 11464/11464);
                      # these entries are for a manual compose run only.
#RELAY_BUFFERS_MAX=   # OPTIONAL, L4-LEGACY: does NOT apply to the phase-1 L7
                      # path, and the build-time sed fails loudly against a
                      # phase-1 ref because the decl is no longer a numeric
                      # literal. Leave empty for L7 runs.
#UPSTREAM_SLOTS_MAX=  # OPTIONAL: build-time overrides of the COMPTIME ceilings —
#CONN_SLOTS_MAX=      # both 11464 by default, pinned equal by zoxy #108 because
                      # an upstream is leased per admitted connection at
                      # saturation, so a conn ceiling above the upstream ceiling
                      # is admission capacity that cannot be served. This is for
                      # pushing PAST the compiled ceiling, not reaching it — use
                      # the runtime knobs above for that. Set both together or
                      # the build fails loudly.
#HEAD_BYTES_MAX_KIB=  # OPTIONAL: build-time override of zoxy's max L7 head, in
                      # KiB (default 8; comptime floor 1). Shrinks the per-slot
                      # footprint — a head over the bound gets 414/431/torn down
                      # instead of served. Fine for this bench's small headers,
                      # not a safe default for arbitrary traffic.
